er=false, source=\"input_text\".\n- If a duration is NOT mentioned, do NOT invent a realistic value. Use exactly:\n  distribution=\"fixed\", value=1.0, unit=\"minutes\", is_placeholder=true, source=\"default_missing_duration\".\n- Apply this rule to every task duration AND to inter_arrival_time.\n- Never invent branch probabilities: include branch_probabilities only if stated in the text; otherwise leave them null and put the decision labels (e.g. \"igen\"/\"nem\") into branch_conditions and the sequence-flow condition_name.\n\nStructural correctness (CRITICAL):\n- Every task and gateway MUST have at least one outgoing and one incoming sequence_flow (unless adjacent to a start/end event).\n- All sequence_flow source_id and target_id values MUST reference existing element IDs.\n- Do NOT leave dead ends or orphans.\n\nPools and message flows (IMPORTANT - do not skip):\n- Whenever the text names two or more distinct organisational units, departments, workshops, roles, or locations that hand work, documents, or material to each other, you MUST model each as a separate pool, and list every element that belongs to it in element_ids. Do not collapse a multi-participant process into a single flat pool.\n- Sequence flows must NEVER cross pool boundaries. Model every hand-over between pools as:\n  message END event in the sending pool -> message_flow -> message START event in the receiving pool.\n- Set trigger_type=\"message\" on those events and give the message a short message_name.\n- Only use a single pool (pools=[]) if the whole process is genuinely performed by one unit.\n\nEvents:\n- event_position is \"start\", \"intermediate\", or \"end\". Use \"intermediate\" for milestones inside a pool (e.g. a phase completed).\n- Use trigger_type=\"message\" only for events that send/receive something across pools.\n\nData perspective (IMPORTANT - do not skip):\n- data_objects: physical or informational ARTEFACTS that flow through the process - documents, drawings, programs, forms, part/tool lists, orders, reports, records, files. Extract every such artefact the text mentions.\n- data_stores: persistent information SYSTEMS or repositories in which data/status is recorded or from which it is retrieved - e.g. MES, ERP, CRM, program server, database, registry, archive, file store. Extract every such system the text mentions.\n- Connect them to tasks: if a task records/writes/updates a system or produces a document, put that data element id into the task's output_data_ids; if it reads/retrieves/uses one, into input_data_ids. Prefer to connect every data element to at least one task.\n- A system that only stores or serves data is a data_store, NOT a resource. Only list it as a resource if it actively performs work.\n\nTask types:\n- Use bpmn:ManualTask for physical work performed by hand, bpmn:ServiceTask for fully automated system actions, bpmn:UserTask for human work done in a software system, and bpmn:Task when unclear.\n- If the text states that a task repeats until a condition is met, set is_loop=true.\n\nReturn the complete ProcessModel as structured output."}, {"role": "human", "content": "After the Expense Report is received, a new account must be created if the employee does not already have one. The report is then reviewed for automatic approval. Amounts under $200 are automatically approved, whereas amounts equal to or over $200 require approval of the supervisor. In case of rejection, the employee must receive a rejection notice by email. Otherwise, the reimbursement goes to the employees direct deposit bank account. If the request is not completed in 7 days, then the employee must receive an approval in progress email. If the request is not finished within 30 days, then the process is stopped and the employee receives an email cancellation notice and must re-submit the expense report."}]}, "finished": "2026-10-02T09:57:13.309+00:00", "latency_s": 17.911, "outcome": "ok", "error": null, "model_returned": "claude-sonnet-5", "finish_re